    "prepomacLinuxIssueComments": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/moritzschuettler/prepomac/issues/2/comments",
      "summary": [
        {
          "date": "2026-10-25T15:40:06Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/moritzschuettler/prepomac/issues/2#issuecomment-6399647971",
          "body": "Hi,\n\nthank you so much \u2013 this is fantastic! I hadn't even thought of Linux, and it's great to see it running on Arch.\n\nYour changes are now in `main` (eb66bf17, with you as co-author), so Linux builds without manual steps:\n\n- **File name case:** the four `mv` you needed are fixed in the project files (macOS ignores case, so I never noticed). A check over all project references found no others.\n- **Native libraries:** `Native/build.sh` builds `libWin32Compat.so` and its `kernel32`/`user32` names on Linux, the projects copy `.so` or `.dylib` depending on the OS, and `GetCurrentThreadId` uses `gettid` there.\n- **NetGenMesher:** takes the OpenCASCADE headers from `/usr/include/opencascade` on Linux, and gmsh from the system or from `GMSH_DIR` (the gmsh SDK, which is what `gmsh-bin` installs).\n- **Mesa:** your shader fallback with `GL_ARB_arrays_of_arrays` is in.\n- **Library lookup:** gmsh (`libgmsh.so`), lp_solve and Python are now also found under their Linux names, so the gmsh mesh items, sweeps and Python scripts work without copying anything.\n\nI checked it in a Debian 13 container (arm64, OpenCASCADE 7.8, gmsh/lp_solve from Debian, Python 3.13): the build, STEP/BREP import, Netgen and gmsh meshing and Python scripts all work without a window. The README has a new \"Linux (experimental)\" section with the steps for Arch and Debian.\n\nYour screenshots also helped the macOS version: the doubled link texts in the About/splash window (\"\u2026MaterialsKIMM - Korean\u2026\") were a bug in the port's LinkLabel and happened on macOS too \u2013 fixed. And the About text no longer says \"on Windows platform\" outside Windows.\n\nTwo things are probably Linux-only and still open: some labels are cut off (e.g. \"Surfaces, edges and vert\" in Set Selection), because the port maps Segoe UI to the macOS system font, which Linux doesn't have, so a wider font is used. And the underscore in \"Vol_S235\" seems to be cut off by the window manager's title bar. If you'd like to look into the font mapping, a pull request is very welcome.\n\nI'm closing this since the build is in \u2013 feel free to reopen or open a new issue if something doesn't work with the current `main`.\n\nThanks again!\nMoritz\n"
        },
        {
          "date": "2026-10-25T16:24:13Z",
          "url": "https://github.com/moritzschuettler/prepomac/issues/2#issuecomment-6400124869",
          "body": "looks great, PrePoMax  reported run flawlessly in Linux. If i can comment, light and shadow in results seems not activated."
        }
      ]
    },
